window.MACGYVER_PACKAGING_PROCESS_CAPTIONS={"version":"34.0.0","status":"PASS","processId":"C01","trackCount":5,"duration":300,"processes":{"C01":{"zh-TW":[{"start":0.0,"end":6.255,"text":"歡迎來到第一道工程活動：定義系統任務與封裝需求。","english":"Welcome to activity one: defining system and package requirements.","speechStart":0.35,"speechEnd":6.074813},{"start":6.255,"end":11.845,"text":"鏡頭下的加速器是教學模型，還沒有選定製造架構。","english":"The accelerator below is a teaching model; its manufacturing architecture has not been selected.","speechStart":6.254812,"speechEnd":11.665062},{"start":11.845,"end":15.619,"text":"今天的成果是一張可追溯需求表。","english":"Our deliverable is a traceable requirements table.","speechStart":11.845062,"speechEnd":15.438771},{"start":15.619,"end":23.036,"text":"你要說清楚它做什麼、在什麼條件下做到，以及用什麼證據判定合格。","english":"State what the system must do, under which conditions, and which evidence will demonstrate success.","speechStart":15.618771,"speechEnd":22.856458},{"start":23.036,"end":30.0,"text":"漂亮的晶片堆疊，不能代替這三個答案。","english":"An impressive stack of chips cannot replace those three answers.","speechStart":23.036458,"speechEnd":26.980687},{"start":30.0,"end":38.746,"text":"先把使用情境寫下來：這個假設的加速器要持續處理資料，不是只跑一秒的展示。","english":"Begin with the use case. Our hypothetical accelerator must process a sustained workload, not a one-second demonstration.","speechStart":30.35,"speechEnd":38.565792},{"start":38.746,"end":46.884,"text":"記錄資料大小、讀寫方向、尖峰與平均需求，還有允許的延遲和運作時間。","english":"Record data size, read and write directions, peak and average demand, allowed latency, and operating duration.","speechStart":38.745792,"speechEnd":46.703771},{"start":46.884,"end":52.212,"text":"畫面中短高柱是突發流量，長平台是持續負載。","english":"The short tall bars represent bursts; the long plateau represents sustained activity.","speechStart":46.883771,"speechEnd":52.031667},{"start":52.212,"end":60.0,"text":"兩者都要描述；只抄介面的最高速率，無法代表應用表現。","english":"Describe both. An interface's headline rate alone does not describe application performance.","speechStart":52.211667,"speechEnd":58.174083},{"start":60.0,"end":66.349,"text":"現在建立四個需求編號：頻寬、散熱、空間與測試。","english":"Create four requirement identifiers: bandwidth, thermal performance, physical envelope, and test access.","speechStart":60.35,"speechEnd":66.169187},{"start":66.349,"end":72.262,"text":"每一列都要有條件、單位、門檻、驗證方法與責任人。","english":"Every row needs conditions, units, a threshold, a verification method, and an owner.","speechStart":66.349187,"speechEnd":72.081896},{"start":72.262,"end":79.268,"text":"比如頻寬這列，要寫單一方向的有效資料率，而不是含糊的很快。","english":"For bandwidth, specify useful data rate in one direction, not simply fast.","speechStart":72.261896,"speechEnd":79.088396},{"start":79.268,"end":83.661,"text":"尚未取得的數字保持待定，指定誰補齊。","english":"Leave unknown values open and assign responsibility for resolving them.","speechStart":79.268396,"speechEnd":83.48075},{"start":83.661,"end":90.0,"text":"提案、估算與實測通過，是三種不同狀態。","english":"A proposal, an estimate, and a measured pass are different states.","speechStart":83.66075,"speechEnd":88.127792},{"start":90.0,"end":100.753,"text":"看這個教學算例：單向六十四條通道，每條每秒十六吉位元，原始總量是一千零二十四吉位元。","english":"Consider this teaching example: sixty-four lanes in one direction, each carrying sixteen gigabits per second. Raw aggregate rate is one thousand twenty-four gigabits per second.","speechStart":90.35,"speechEnd":100.572542},{"start":100.753,"end":109.973,"text":"假設協定與負載合計效率八成，再除以八換成位元組，得到每秒一百零二點四吉位元組。","english":"Assume eighty percent combined protocol and workload efficiency; divide by eight to obtain one hundred two point four gigabytes per second.","speechStart":100.752542,"speechEnd":109.792771},{"start":109.973,"end":120.0,"text":"這不是任何標準的保證規格；效率、方向與流量型態，都必須另外驗證。","english":"This is arithmetic, not a standards guarantee. Verify efficiency, direction, and traffic conditions separately.","speechStart":109.972771,"speechEnd":117.448021},{"start":120.0,"end":123.23,"text":"散熱也先做有條件的估算。","english":"Start thermal planning with explicit assumptions.","speechStart":120.35,"speechEnd":123.049792},{"start":123.23,"end":132.685,"text":"假設持續功率二百五十瓦，完整冷卻系統的有效熱阻是每瓦零點一八度，環境三十五度。","english":"Assume two hundred fifty watts sustained, an effective resistance of zero point one eight kelvin per watt for the complete cooling system, and thirty-five degrees ambient.","speechStart":123.229792,"speechEnd":132.504771},{"start":132.685,"end":138.683,"text":"簡化穩態估算得到八十度，比假設上限八十五度低五度。","english":"A lumped steady-state estimate gives eighty degrees, five below our illustrative limit.","speechStart":132.684771,"speechEnd":138.502792},{"start":138.683,"end":141.764,"text":"但這不是最熱晶粒的驗證結果。","english":"That is not verified peak junction temperature.","speechStart":138.682792,"speechEnd":141.584396},{"start":141.764,"end":150.0,"text":"接面、氣流、局部功率與暫態，都還需要建模和量測。","english":"Interfaces, airflow, local power, and transients still require modeling and measurement.","speechStart":141.764396,"speechEnd":147.511937},{"start":150.0,"end":152.496,"text":"把視角拉到主機板。","english":"Pull back to the board.","speechStart":150.35,"speechEnd":152.316396},{"start":152.496,"end":161.383,"text":"案例暫留六十乘六十毫米、封裝本體高四毫米的空間，散熱器和固定件要另外計算。","english":"Reserve sixty by sixty millimeters and four millimeters of package-body height in this example; budget the cooler and mounting hardware separately.","speechStart":152.496396,"speechEnd":161.203167},{"start":161.383,"end":168.75,"text":"再畫出電源進入晶粒的路徑，指定供電範圍、壓降預算與量測位置。","english":"Trace power into the dies, and specify supply range, voltage-drop budget, and measurement points.","speechStart":161.383167,"speechEnd":168.569521},{"start":168.75,"end":180.0,"text":"小封裝不一定帶來小系統；插座、電容、走線和維修空間，都會改變最後布局。","english":"A smaller package does not automatically make a smaller system. Sockets, capacitors, routing, and service clearances affect the layout.","speechStart":168.749521,"speechEnd":177.491521},{"start":180.0,"end":184.221,"text":"在晶粒被蓋住之前，決定怎麼觀察故障。","english":"Before a die becomes inaccessible, decide how faults will be observed.","speechStart":180.35,"speechEnd":184.040542},{"start":184.221,"end":190.036,"text":"先確認裸晶的測試資料，再規劃組裝後的連線與功能測試。","english":"Review incoming die-test evidence, then plan interconnect and functional tests after assembly.","speechStart":184.220542,"speechEnd":189.855917},{"start":190.036,"end":195.854,"text":"畫面的探針代表可控制、可觀測的入口，不是實際探針尺寸。","english":"The probes symbolize controllable, observable access; their size is illustrative.","speechStart":190.035917,"speechEnd":195.673563},{"start":195.854,"end":199.016,"text":"測不到的內部節點不能假裝正常。","english":"An unobservable internal node cannot simply be assumed good.","speechStart":195.853563,"speechEnd":198.835896},{"start":199.016,"end":210.0,"text":"需求表要交代故障範圍、測試階段與資料歸屬，避免昂貴組裝後才發現缺口。","english":"Record fault scope, test stage, and data ownership, so expensive integration does not reveal a missing test strategy.","speechStart":199.015896,"speechEnd":206.858354},{"start":210.0,"end":212.757,"text":"現在才比較候選架構。","english":"Now compare candidate architectures.","speechStart":210.35,"speechEnd":212.576854},{"start":212.757,"end":222.928,"text":"矽中介層、扇出重佈線與局部矽橋，是不同的互連路線；垂直混合鍵合還可能與其中某些路線組合。","english":"Silicon interposers, fan-out redistribution, and local silicon bridges provide different interconnect routes. Vertical hybrid bonding can also combine with some routes.","speechStart":212.756854,"speechEnd":222.748063},{"start":222.928,"end":226.853,"text":"不要把它們排成每個產品都必經的流水線。","english":"Do not turn them into a mandatory serial factory line.","speechStart":222.928063,"speechEnd":226.67325},{"start":226.853,"end":233.146,"text":"比較有效頻寬、功率、尺寸、測試能力、供應條件與總成本。","english":"Compare useful bandwidth, power, dimensions, test access, supply conditions, and total cost.","speechStart":226.85325,"speechEnd":232.966042},{"start":233.146,"end":240.0,"text":"此刻保留候選，先列出需要證明的差異。","english":"Keep alternatives open while identifying the evidence needed to distinguish them.","speechStart":233.146042,"speechEnd":237.158667},{"start":240.0,"end":252.554,"text":"試著破壞剛才的假設：若實際冷卻系統有效熱阻變成每瓦零點二二度，同樣功率下，簡化估算就升到九十度，超過案例門檻。","english":"Challenge the cooling assumption. If effective system resistance rises to zero point two two kelvin per watt, the same screening calculation reaches ninety degrees, exceeding our example limit.","speechStart":240.35,"speechEnd":252.374083},{"start":252.554,"end":256.863,"text":"這是待解決的風險，不是漂亮動畫中的通過。","english":"That is an unresolved risk, not an animated pass.","speechStart":252.554083,"speechEnd":256.683208},{"start":256.863,"end":263.61,"text":"保存模型版本、邊界條件、量測位置與誤差，再比較持續吞吐量。","english":"Preserve model revision, boundary conditions, measurement locations, and uncertainty. Then check sustained throughput.","speechStart":256.863208,"speechEnd":263.429708},{"start":263.61,"end":270.0,"text":"降頻後的速度，也必須算進需求驗證。","english":"Any performance reduction from thermal throttling belongs in the verification result.","speechStart":263.609708,"speechEnd":267.160104},{"start":270.0,"end":272.101,"text":"最後回到全貌。","english":"Return to the complete system.","speechStart":270.35,"speechEnd":271.920813},{"start":272.101,"end":277.35,"text":"你交付的是有版本的需求基線，以及仍未解決的事項。","english":"Deliver a versioned requirements baseline and an explicit open-issues list.","speechStart":272.100813,"speechEnd":277.169854},{"start":277.35,"end":285.076,"text":"每項關鍵需求，都要連到負責人和驗證證據；還沒量到的，維持待驗證。","english":"Link each critical requirement to an owner and its verification evidence; unmeasured items remain unverified.","speechStart":277.349854,"speechEnd":284.896125},{"start":285.076,"end":291.65,"text":"下一道活動是功能與晶粒分割，把需求轉成候選系統構成。","english":"Next comes functional and die partitioning, turning requirements into candidate system compositions.","speechStart":285.076125,"speechEnd":291.469646},{"start":291.65,"end":300.0,"text":"先問清楚成功的條件，後面的每一道製造與測試，才知道要證明什麼。","english":"Defining success first gives every later manufacturing and testing activity a clear purpose and a claim to demonstrate.","speechStart":291.649646,"speechEnd":298.72725}],"zh-CN":[{"start":0.0,"end":6.283,"text":"欢迎来到第一道工程活动：定义系统任务与封装需求。","english":"Welcome to activity one: defining system and package requirements.","speechStart":0.35,"speechEnd":6.103292},{"start":6.283,"end":12.165,"text":"镜头下的加速器是教学模型，还没有选定制造架构。","english":"The accelerator below is a teaching model; its manufacturing architecture has not been selected.","speechStart":6.283292,"speechEnd":11.985167},{"start":12.165,"end":15.875,"text":"今天的成果是一张可追溯需求表。","english":"Our deliverable is a traceable requirements table.","speechStart":12.165167,"speechEnd":15.695333},{"start":15.875,"end":23.537,"text":"你要说清楚它做什么、在什么条件下做到，以及用什么证据判定合格。","english":"State what the system must do, under which conditions, and which evidence will demonstrate success.","speechStart":15.875333,"speechEnd":23.35675},{"start":23.537,"end":30.0,"text":"漂亮的芯片堆叠，不能代替这三个答案。","english":"An impressive stack of chips cannot replace those three answers.","speechStart":23.53675,"speechEnd":27.861792},{"start":30.0,"end":38.405,"text":"先把使用情境写下来：这个假设的加速器要持续处理数据，不是只跑一秒的展示。","english":"Begin with the use case. Our hypothetical accelerator must process a sustained workload, not a one-second demonstration.","speechStart":30.35,"speechEnd":38.225062},{"start":38.405,"end":46.288,"text":"记录数据大小、读写方向、峰值与平均需求，还有允许的延迟和运行时间。","english":"Record data size, read and write directions, peak and average demand, allowed latency, and operating duration.","speechStart":38.405062,"speechEnd":46.10775},{"start":46.288,"end":51.386,"text":"画面中短高柱是突发流量，长平台是持续负载。","english":"The short tall bars represent bursts; the long plateau represents sustained activity.","speechStart":46.28775,"speechEnd":51.2065},{"start":51.386,"end":60.0,"text":"两者都要描述；只抄接口的最高速率，无法代表应用表现。","english":"Describe both. An interface's headline rate alone does not describe application performance.","speechStart":51.3865,"speechEnd":57.167604},{"start":60.0,"end":66.13,"text":"现在建立四个需求编号：带宽、散热、空间与测试。","english":"Create four requirement identifiers: bandwidth, thermal performance, physical envelope, and test access.","speechStart":60.35,"speechEnd":65.95},{"start":66.13,"end":71.977,"text":"每一行都要有条件、单位、门槛、验证方法与负责人。","english":"Every row needs conditions, units, a threshold, a verification method, and an owner.","speechStart":66.13,"speechEnd":71.797167},{"start":71.977,"end":78.548,"text":"比如带宽这一行，要写单一方向的有效数据率，而不是含糊的很快。","english":"For bandwidth, specify useful data rate in one direction, not simply fast.","speechStart":71.977167,"speechEnd":78.368146},{"start":78.548,"end":82.645,"text":"尚未取得的数字保持待定，指定谁补齐。","english":"Leave unknown values open and assign responsibility for resolving them.","speechStart":78.548146,"speechEnd":82.465292},{"start":82.645,"end":90.0,"text":"提案、估算与实测通过，是三种不同状态。","english":"A proposal, an estimate, and a measured pass are different states.","speechStart":82.645292,"speechEnd":87.079083},{"start":90.0,"end":100.987,"text":"看这个教学算例：单向六十四条通道，每条每秒十六吉比特，原始总量是一千零二十四吉比特。","english":"Consider this teaching example: sixty-four lanes in one direction, each carrying sixteen gigabits per second. Raw aggregate rate is one thousand twenty-four gigabits per second.","speechStart":90.35,"speechEnd":100.806979},{"start":100.987,"end":110.338,"text":"假设协议与负载合计效率八成，再除以八换成字节，得到每秒一百零二点四吉字节。","english":"Assume eighty percent combined protocol and workload efficiency; divide by eight to obtain one hundred two point four gigabytes per second.","speechStart":100.986979,"speechEnd":110.157958},{"start":110.338,"end":120.0,"text":"这不是任何标准的保证规格；效率、方向与流量类型，都必须另外验证。","english":"This is arithmetic, not a standards guarantee. Verify efficiency, direction, and traffic conditions separately.","speechStart":110.337958,"speechEnd":118.347583},{"start":120.0,"end":123.376,"text":"散热也先做有条件的估算。","english":"Start thermal planning with explicit assumptions.","speechStart":120.35,"speechEnd":123.196354},{"start":123.376,"end":132.942,"text":"假设持续功率二百五十瓦，完整冷却系统的有效热阻是每瓦零点一八度，环境三十五度。","english":"Assume two hundred fifty watts sustained, an effective resistance of zero point one eight kelvin per watt for the complete cooling system, and thirty-five degrees ambient.","speechStart":123.376354,"speechEnd":132.761937},{"start":132.942,"end":139.181,"text":"简化稳态估算得到八十度，比假设上限八十五度低五度。","english":"A lumped steady-state estimate gives eighty degrees, five below our illustrative limit.","speechStart":132.941937,"speechEnd":139.001042},{"start":139.181,"end":142.373,"text":"但这不是最热芯粒的验证结果。","english":"That is not verified peak junction temperature.","speechStart":139.181042,"speechEnd":142.193333},{"start":142.373,"end":150.0,"text":"界面、气流、局部功率与瞬态，都还需要建模和测量。","english":"Interfaces, airflow, local power, and transients still require modeling and measurement.","speechStart":142.373333,"speechEnd":148.553333},{"start":150.0,"end":152.223,"text":"把视角拉到主板。","english":"Pull back to the board.","speechStart":150.35,"speechEnd":152.043208},{"start":152.223,"end":161.746,"text":"案例暂留六十乘六十毫米、封装本体高四毫米的空间，散热器和固定件要另外计算。","english":"Reserve sixty by sixty millimeters and four millimeters of package-body height in this example; budget the cooler and mounting hardware separately.","speechStart":152.223208,"speechEnd":161.566083},{"start":161.746,"end":169.248,"text":"再画出电源进入芯粒的路径，指定供电范围、压降预算与测量位置。","english":"Trace power into the dies, and specify supply range, voltage-drop budget, and measurement points.","speechStart":161.746083,"speechEnd":169.067688},{"start":169.248,"end":180.0,"text":"小封装不一定带来小系统；插座、电容、走线和维修空间，都会改变最后布局。","english":"A smaller package does not automatically make a smaller system. Sockets, capacitors, routing, and service clearances affect the layout.","speechStart":169.247688,"speechEnd":178.649104},{"start":180.0,"end":184.419,"text":"在芯粒被盖住之前，决定怎么观察故障。","english":"Before a die becomes inaccessible, decide how faults will be observed.","speechStart":180.35,"speechEnd":184.238542},{"start":184.419,"end":190.347,"text":"先确认裸芯的测试数据，再规划组装后的连线与功能测试。","english":"Review incoming die-test evidence, then plan interconnect and functional tests after assembly.","speechStart":184.418542,"speechEnd":190.167208},{"start":190.347,"end":196.611,"text":"画面的探针代表可控制、可观察的入口，不是实际探针尺寸。","english":"The probes symbolize controllable, observable access; their size is illustrative.","speechStart":190.347208,"speechEnd":196.431292},{"start":196.611,"end":199.872,"text":"测不到的内部节点不能假装正常。","english":"An unobservable internal node cannot simply be assumed good.","speechStart":196.611292,"speechEnd":199.691937},{"start":199.872,"end":210.0,"text":"需求表要交代故障范围、测试阶段与数据归属，避免昂贵组装后才发现缺口。","english":"Record fault scope, test stage, and data ownership, so expensive integration does not reveal a missing test strategy.","speechStart":199.871938,"speechEnd":207.866646},{"start":210.0,"end":212.785,"text":"现在才比较候选架构。","english":"Now compare candidate architectures.","speechStart":210.35,"speechEnd":212.604979},{"start":212.785,"end":223.343,"text":"硅中介层、扇出重布线与局部硅桥，是不同的互连路线；垂直混合键合还可能与其中某些路线组合。","english":"Silicon interposers, fan-out redistribution, and local silicon bridges provide different interconnect routes. Vertical hybrid bonding can also combine with some routes.","speechStart":212.784979,"speechEnd":223.163229},{"start":223.343,"end":227.486,"text":"不要把它们排成每个产品都必经的流水线。","english":"Do not turn them into a mandatory serial factory line.","speechStart":223.343229,"speechEnd":227.305688},{"start":227.486,"end":234.09,"text":"比较有效带宽、功率、尺寸、测试能力、供应条件与总成本。","english":"Compare useful bandwidth, power, dimensions, test access, supply conditions, and total cost.","speechStart":227.485688,"speechEnd":233.910229},{"start":234.09,"end":240.0,"text":"此刻保留候选，先列出需要证明的差异。","english":"Keep alternatives open while identifying the evidence needed to distinguish them.","speechStart":234.090229,"speechEnd":238.144937},{"start":240.0,"end":253.348,"text":"试着破坏刚才的假设：若实际冷却系统有效热阻变成每瓦零点二二度，同样功率下，简化估算就升到九十度，超过案例门槛。","english":"Challenge the cooling assumption. If effective system resistance rises to zero point two two kelvin per watt, the same screening calculation reaches ninety degrees, exceeding our example limit.","speechStart":240.35,"speechEnd":253.167917},{"start":253.348,"end":257.748,"text":"这是待解决的风险，不是漂亮动画中的通过。","english":"That is an unresolved risk, not an animated pass.","speechStart":253.347917,"speechEnd":257.568333},{"start":257.748,"end":264.816,"text":"保存模型版本、边界条件、测量位置与误差，再比较持续吞吐量。","english":"Preserve model revision, boundary conditions, measurement locations, and uncertainty. Then check sustained throughput.","speechStart":257.748333,"speechEnd":264.6355},{"start":264.816,"end":270.0,"text":"降频后的速度，也必须算进需求验证。","english":"Any performance reduction from thermal throttling belongs in the verification result.","speechStart":264.8155,"speechEnd":268.549062},{"start":270.0,"end":272.002,"text":"最后回到全貌。","english":"Return to the complete system.","speechStart":270.35,"speechEnd":271.822021},{"start":272.002,"end":277.043,"text":"你交付的是有版本的需求基线，以及仍未解决的事项。","english":"Deliver a versioned requirements baseline and an explicit open-issues list.","speechStart":272.002021,"speechEnd":276.863021},{"start":277.043,"end":284.428,"text":"每项关键需求，都要连到负责人和验证证据；还没测到的，维持待验证。","english":"Link each critical requirement to an owner and its verification evidence; unmeasured items remain unverified.","speechStart":277.043021,"speechEnd":284.247604},{"start":284.428,"end":290.638,"text":"下一道活动是功能与芯粒划分，把需求转成候选系统构成。","english":"Next comes functional and die partitioning, turning requirements into candidate system compositions.","speechStart":284.427604,"speechEnd":290.457812},{"start":290.638,"end":300.0,"text":"先问清楚成功的条件，后面的每一道制造与测试，才知道要证明什么。","english":"Defining success first gives every later manufacturing and testing activity a clear purpose and a claim to demonstrate.","speechStart":290.637812,"speechEnd":297.390062}],"en":[{"start":0.0,"end":5.551,"text":"Welcome to activity one: defining system and package requirements.","english":"","speechStart":0.35,"speechEnd":5.371417},{"start":5.551,"end":12.196,"text":"The accelerator below is a teaching model; its manufacturing architecture has not been selected.","english":"","speechStart":5.551417,"speechEnd":12.016458},{"start":12.196,"end":15.742,"text":"Our deliverable is a traceable requirements table.","english":"","speechStart":12.196458,"speechEnd":15.562042},{"start":15.742,"end":22.634,"text":"State what the system must do, under which conditions, and which evidence will demonstrate success.","english":"","speechStart":15.742042,"speechEnd":22.454062},{"start":22.634,"end":30.0,"text":"An impressive stack of chips cannot replace those three answers.","english":"","speechStart":22.634062,"speechEnd":26.677437},{"start":30.0,"end":32.002,"text":"Begin with the use case.","english":"","speechStart":30.35,"speechEnd":31.821979},{"start":32.002,"end":38.247,"text":"Our hypothetical accelerator must process a sustained workload, not a one-second demonstration.","english":"","speechStart":32.001979,"speechEnd":38.066792},{"start":38.247,"end":46.096,"text":"Record data size, read and write directions, peak and average demand, allowed latency, and operating duration.","english":"","speechStart":38.246792,"speechEnd":45.916104},{"start":46.096,"end":51.818,"text":"The short tall bars represent bursts; the long plateau represents sustained activity.","english":"","speechStart":46.096104,"speechEnd":51.638104},{"start":51.818,"end":52.993,"text":"Describe both.","english":"","speechStart":51.818104,"speechEnd":52.812854},{"start":52.993,"end":60.0,"text":"An interface's headline rate alone does not describe application performance.","english":"","speechStart":52.992854,"speechEnd":57.708917},{"start":60.0,"end":67.766,"text":"Create four requirement identifiers: bandwidth, thermal performance, physical envelope, and test access.","english":"","speechStart":60.35,"speechEnd":67.586208},{"start":67.766,"end":73.546,"text":"Every row needs conditions, units, a threshold, a verification method, and an owner.","english":"","speechStart":67.766208,"speechEnd":73.366042},{"start":73.546,"end":78.784,"text":"For bandwidth, specify useful data rate in one direction, not simply fast.","english":"","speechStart":73.546042,"speechEnd":78.604021},{"start":78.784,"end":82.916,"text":"Leave unknown values open and assign responsibility for resolving them.","english":"","speechStart":78.784021,"speechEnd":82.736312},{"start":82.916,"end":90.0,"text":"A proposal, an estimate, and a measured pass are different states.","english":"","speechStart":82.916313,"speechEnd":86.741312},{"start":90.0,"end":97.754,"text":"Consider this teaching example: sixty-four lanes in one direction, each carrying sixteen gigabits per second.","english":"","speechStart":90.35,"speechEnd":97.573771},{"start":97.754,"end":101.834,"text":"Raw aggregate rate is one thousand twenty-four gigabits per second.","english":"","speechStart":97.753771,"speechEnd":101.654458},{"start":101.834,"end":110.552,"text":"Assume eighty percent combined protocol and workload efficiency; divide by eight to obtain one hundred two point four gigabytes per second.","english":"","speechStart":101.834458,"speechEnd":110.371604},{"start":110.552,"end":113.849,"text":"This is arithmetic, not a standards guarantee.","english":"","speechStart":110.551604,"speechEnd":113.669083},{"start":113.849,"end":120.0,"text":"Verify efficiency, direction, and traffic conditions separately.","english":"","speechStart":113.849083,"speechEnd":118.350958},{"start":120.0,"end":133.389,"text":"Start thermal planning with explicit assumptions: two hundred fifty watts sustained, an effective resistance of zero point one eight kelvin per watt for the complete cooling system, and thirty-five degrees ambient.","english":"","speechStart":120.35,"speechEnd":133.208521},{"start":133.389,"end":138.693,"text":"A lumped steady-state estimate gives eighty degrees, five below our illustrative limit.","english":"","speechStart":133.388521,"speechEnd":138.513438},{"start":138.693,"end":141.635,"text":"That is not verified peak junction temperature.","english":"","speechStart":138.693438,"speechEnd":141.455437},{"start":141.635,"end":150.0,"text":"Interfaces, airflow, local power, and transients still require modeling and measurement.","english":"","speechStart":141.635437,"speechEnd":147.581562},{"start":150.0,"end":151.774,"text":"Pull back to the board.","english":"","speechStart":150.35,"speechEnd":151.594458},{"start":151.774,"end":160.667,"text":"Reserve sixty by sixty millimeters and four millimeters of package-body height in this example; budget the cooler and mounting hardware separately.","english":"","speechStart":151.774458,"speechEnd":160.487167},{"start":160.667,"end":167.679,"text":"Trace power into the dies, and specify supply range, voltage-drop budget, and measurement points.","english":"","speechStart":160.667167,"speechEnd":167.498521},{"start":167.679,"end":171.729,"text":"A smaller package does not automatically make a smaller system.","english":"","speechStart":167.678521,"speechEnd":171.549062},{"start":171.729,"end":180.0,"text":"Sockets, capacitors, routing, and service clearances affect the layout.","english":"","speechStart":171.729062,"speechEnd":176.939104},{"start":180.0,"end":184.949,"text":"Before a die becomes inaccessible, decide how faults will be observed.","english":"","speechStart":180.35,"speechEnd":184.769187},{"start":184.949,"end":191.053,"text":"Review incoming die-test evidence, then plan interconnect and functional tests after assembly.","english":"","speechStart":184.949187,"speechEnd":190.873104},{"start":191.053,"end":196.442,"text":"The probes symbolize controllable, observable access; their size is illustrative.","english":"","speechStart":191.053104,"speechEnd":196.261542},{"start":196.442,"end":200.151,"text":"An unobservable internal node cannot simply be assumed good.","english":"","speechStart":196.441542,"speechEnd":199.970854},{"start":200.151,"end":210.0,"text":"Record fault scope, test stage, and data ownership, so expensive integration does not reveal a missing test strategy.","english":"","speechStart":200.150854,"speechEnd":208.397312},{"start":210.0,"end":212.665,"text":"Now compare candidate architectures.","english":"","speechStart":210.35,"speechEnd":212.484938},{"start":212.665,"end":219.35,"text":"Silicon interposers, fan-out redistribution, and local silicon bridges provide different interconnect routes.","english":"","speechStart":212.664938,"speechEnd":219.17025},{"start":219.35,"end":222.734,"text":"Vertical hybrid bonding can also combine with some routes.","english":"","speechStart":219.35025,"speechEnd":222.553896},{"start":222.734,"end":226.155,"text":"Do not turn them into a mandatory serial factory line.","english":"","speechStart":222.733896,"speechEnd":225.975396},{"start":226.155,"end":233.247,"text":"Compare useful bandwidth, power, dimensions, test access, supply conditions, and total cost.","english":"","speechStart":226.155396,"speechEnd":233.066792},{"start":233.247,"end":240.0,"text":"Keep alternatives open while identifying the evidence needed to distinguish them.","english":"","speechStart":233.246792,"speechEnd":237.652104},{"start":240.0,"end":242.125,"text":"Challenge the cooling assumption.","english":"","speechStart":240.35,"speechEnd":241.945021},{"start":242.125,"end":251.735,"text":"If effective system resistance rises to zero point two two kelvin per watt, the same screening calculation reaches ninety degrees, exceeding our example limit.","english":"","speechStart":242.125021,"speechEnd":251.555229},{"start":251.735,"end":254.996,"text":"That is an unresolved risk, not an animated pass.","english":"","speechStart":251.735229,"speechEnd":254.816229},{"start":254.996,"end":260.579,"text":"Preserve model revision, boundary conditions, measurement locations, and uncertainty.","english":"","speechStart":254.996229,"speechEnd":260.399333},{"start":260.579,"end":270.0,"text":"Then check sustained throughput; any performance reduction from thermal throttling belongs in the verification result.","english":"","speechStart":260.579333,"speechEnd":266.805063},{"start":270.0,"end":272.366,"text":"Return to the complete system.","english":"","speechStart":270.35,"speechEnd":272.185708},{"start":272.366,"end":277.121,"text":"Deliver a versioned requirements baseline and an explicit open-issues list.","english":"","speechStart":272.365708,"speechEnd":276.940729},{"start":277.121,"end":284.38,"text":"Link each critical requirement to an owner and its verification evidence; unmeasured items remain unverified.","english":"","speechStart":277.120729,"speechEnd":284.200333},{"start":284.38,"end":290.912,"text":"Next comes functional and die partitioning, turning requirements into candidate system compositions.","english":"","speechStart":284.380333,"speechEnd":290.731688},{"start":290.912,"end":300.0,"text":"Defining success first gives every later manufacturing and testing activity a clear purpose and a claim to demonstrate.","english":"","speechStart":290.911687,"speechEnd":298.073146}],"ja":[{"start":0.0,"end":5.897,"text":"最初の活動は、システムの役割とパッケージ要件の定義です。","english":"Welcome to activity one: defining system and package requirements.","speechStart":0.35,"speechEnd":5.716854},{"start":5.897,"end":12.186,"text":"このアクセラレーターは教材用モデルで、製造構造はまだ未選定です。","english":"The accelerator below is a teaching model; its manufacturing architecture has not been selected.","speechStart":5.896854,"speechEnd":12.005625},{"start":12.186,"end":16.786,"text":"成果物は、根拠を追跡できる要件表です。","english":"Our deliverable is a traceable requirements table.","speechStart":12.185625,"speechEnd":16.606125},{"start":16.786,"end":22.933,"text":"何を実現し、どの条件で動かし、どの証拠で合格と判断するか。","english":"State what the system must do, under which conditions, and which evidence will demonstrate success.","speechStart":16.786125,"speechEnd":22.753125},{"start":22.933,"end":30.0,"text":"この三つの答えは、美しいチップの積層だけでは得られません。","english":"An impressive stack of chips cannot replace those three answers.","speechStart":22.933125,"speechEnd":28.010958},{"start":30.0,"end":32.494,"text":"まず使用場面を記述します。","english":"Begin with the use case.","speechStart":30.35,"speechEnd":32.314354},{"start":32.494,"end":38.111,"text":"この仮想アクセラレーターには、一秒の実演ではなく、継続処理が必要です。","english":"Our hypothetical accelerator must process a sustained workload, not a one-second demonstration.","speechStart":32.494354,"speechEnd":37.931188},{"start":38.111,"end":44.273,"text":"データ量、読み書きの方向、ピークと平均、許容遅延、運転時間を記録します。","english":"Record data size, read and write directions, peak and average demand, allowed latency, and operating duration.","speechStart":38.111187,"speechEnd":44.092833},{"start":44.273,"end":49.004,"text":"高く短い棒は突発的な負荷、長い台地は持続負荷です。","english":"The short tall bars represent bursts; the long plateau represents sustained activity.","speechStart":44.272833,"speechEnd":48.824458},{"start":49.004,"end":50.757,"text":"両方を定義しましょう。","english":"Describe both.","speechStart":49.004458,"speechEnd":50.577354},{"start":50.757,"end":60.0,"text":"接続仕様の最高速度だけでは、実際の処理性能を表せません。","english":"An interface's headline rate alone does not describe application performance.","speechStart":50.757354,"speechEnd":55.707062},{"start":60.0,"end":65.405,"text":"帯域、放熱、寸法、テストの四つに要件番号を付けます。","english":"Create four requirement identifiers: bandwidth, thermal performance, physical envelope, and test access.","speechStart":60.35,"speechEnd":65.22525},{"start":65.405,"end":71.499,"text":"各行には、条件、単位、基準値、検証方法、担当者が必要です。","english":"Every row needs conditions, units, a threshold, a verification method, and an owner.","speechStart":65.40525,"speechEnd":71.318542},{"start":71.499,"end":76.917,"text":"帯域なら、単に高速とせず、一方向の有効データ速度を指定します。","english":"For bandwidth, specify useful data rate in one direction, not simply fast.","speechStart":71.498542,"speechEnd":76.737104},{"start":76.917,"end":80.793,"text":"不明な数値は未決のまま、確認担当を決めます。","english":"Leave unknown values open and assign responsibility for resolving them.","speechStart":76.917104,"speechEnd":80.612813},{"start":80.793,"end":90.0,"text":"提案、概算、実測による合格は、区別して管理してください。","english":"A proposal, an estimate, and a measured pass are different states.","speechStart":80.792812,"speechEnd":85.867917},{"start":90.0,"end":92.393,"text":"教材の計算例です。","english":"Consider this teaching example.","speechStart":90.35,"speechEnd":92.212875},{"start":92.393,"end":96.956,"text":"一方向に六十四レーン、各レーンは毎秒十六ギガビット。","english":"Sixty-four lanes in one direction, each carrying sixteen gigabits per second.","speechStart":92.392875,"speechEnd":96.775688},{"start":96.956,"end":100.61,"text":"生の合計は毎秒千二十四ギガビットです。","english":"Raw aggregate rate is one thousand twenty-four gigabits per second.","speechStart":96.955687,"speechEnd":100.429667},{"start":100.61,"end":109.597,"text":"通信規約と負荷を合わせた効率を八割と仮定し、八で割ってバイトにすると、毎秒百二点四ギガバイトになります。","english":"Assume eighty percent combined protocol and workload efficiency; divide by eight to obtain one hundred two point four gigabytes per second.","speechStart":100.609667,"speechEnd":109.417063},{"start":109.597,"end":112.439,"text":"規格が保証する値ではありません。","english":"This is not a standards guarantee.","speechStart":109.597062,"speechEnd":112.259062},{"start":112.439,"end":120.0,"text":"効率、方向、通信条件は別途検証します。","english":"Verify efficiency, direction, and traffic conditions separately.","speechStart":112.439063,"speechEnd":116.717854},{"start":120.0,"end":122.732,"text":"熱も条件を明示して概算します。","english":"Start thermal planning with explicit assumptions.","speechStart":120.35,"speechEnd":122.551563},{"start":122.732,"end":130.546,"text":"持続電力二百五十ワット、冷却系全体の有効熱抵抗を一ワット当たり零点一八度、周囲を三十五度と仮定します。","english":"Assume two hundred fifty watts sustained, an effective resistance of zero point one eight kelvin per watt for the complete cooling system, and thirty-five degrees ambient.","speechStart":122.731562,"speechEnd":130.366167},{"start":130.546,"end":135.977,"text":"集中定数の定常計算は八十度で、仮の上限八十五度より五度低い値です。","english":"A lumped steady-state estimate gives eighty degrees, five below our illustrative limit.","speechStart":130.546167,"speechEnd":135.796875},{"start":135.977,"end":138.808,"text":"ただし最高接合温度の検証ではありません。","english":"That is not verified peak junction temperature.","speechStart":135.976875,"speechEnd":138.628458},{"start":138.808,"end":150.0,"text":"界面、気流、局所電力、過渡状態を解析し、測定する必要があります。","english":"Interfaces, airflow, local power, and transients still require modeling and measurement.","speechStart":138.808458,"speechEnd":143.751146},{"start":150.0,"end":152.224,"text":"基板全体を見ましょう。","english":"Pull back to the board.","speechStart":150.35,"speechEnd":152.044292},{"start":152.224,"end":160.132,"text":"この例では、本体用に六十ミリ四方、高さ四ミリを確保し、冷却器や固定具は別に計上します。","english":"Reserve sixty by sixty millimeters and four millimeters of package-body height in this example; budget the cooler and mounting hardware separately.","speechStart":152.224292,"speechEnd":159.952292},{"start":160.132,"end":166.723,"text":"電源がダイへ入る経路を描き、供給範囲、電圧降下の予算、測定点を指定します。","english":"Trace power into the dies, and specify supply range, voltage-drop budget, and measurement points.","speechStart":160.132292,"speechEnd":166.542646},{"start":166.723,"end":171.102,"text":"小さなパッケージが、小さなシステムを意味するとは限りません。","english":"A smaller package does not automatically make a smaller system.","speechStart":166.722646,"speechEnd":170.922167},{"start":171.102,"end":180.0,"text":"ソケット、容量部品、配線、保守空間も配置を左右します。","english":"Sockets, capacitors, routing, and service clearances affect the layout.","speechStart":171.102167,"speechEnd":175.684042},{"start":180.0,"end":183.783,"text":"ダイが隠れる前に、故障の観測方法を決めます。","english":"Before a die becomes inaccessible, decide how faults will be observed.","speechStart":180.35,"speechEnd":183.60275},{"start":183.783,"end":189.811,"text":"受け入れ時のダイ試験の証拠を確認し、組立後の接続試験と機能試験を計画します。","english":"Review incoming die-test evidence, then plan interconnect and functional tests after assembly.","speechStart":183.78275,"speechEnd":189.630833},{"start":189.811,"end":194.458,"text":"探針は制御と観測の入口を示す記号で、実寸ではありません。","english":"The probes symbolize controllable, observable access; their size is illustrative.","speechStart":189.810833,"speechEnd":194.277958},{"start":194.458,"end":198.097,"text":"観測できない内部点を、良品とみなしてはいけません。","english":"An unobservable internal node cannot simply be assumed good.","speechStart":194.457958,"speechEnd":197.917417},{"start":198.097,"end":210.0,"text":"故障範囲、試験段階、データの担当を記録し、高価な組立後に不足が判明するのを防ぎます。","english":"Record fault scope, test stage, and data ownership, so expensive integration does not reveal a missing test strategy.","speechStart":198.097417,"speechEnd":204.6065},{"start":210.0,"end":212.637,"text":"ここで候補構造を比較します。","english":"Now compare candidate architectures.","speechStart":210.35,"speechEnd":212.457125},{"start":212.637,"end":218.408,"text":"シリコンインターポーザー、ファンアウト配線、局所シリコンブリッジは、異なる接続経路です。","english":"Silicon interposers, fan-out redistribution, and local silicon bridges provide different interconnect routes.","speechStart":212.637125,"speechEnd":218.22775},{"start":218.408,"end":222.36,"text":"垂直ハイブリッド接合は、一部と組み合わせることもできます。","english":"Vertical hybrid bonding can also combine with some routes.","speechStart":218.40775,"speechEnd":222.180042},{"start":222.36,"end":225.724,"text":"すべてを必須の連続工程に並べてはいけません。","english":"Do not turn them into a mandatory serial factory line.","speechStart":222.360042,"speechEnd":225.544396},{"start":225.724,"end":240.0,"text":"有効帯域、電力、寸法、試験性、供給条件、総費用を比べ、候補の差を証明するために必要な証拠を整理します。","english":"Compare useful bandwidth, power, dimensions, test access, supply conditions, and total cost; identify the evidence needed to distinguish candidates.","speechStart":225.724396,"speechEnd":234.673708},{"start":240.0,"end":242.348,"text":"冷却の仮定を変えてみます。","english":"Challenge the cooling assumption.","speechStart":240.35,"speechEnd":242.167875},{"start":242.348,"end":250.601,"text":"有効熱抵抗が一ワット当たり零点二二度になると、同じ電力でも概算は九十度となり、教材の上限を超えます。","english":"If effective system resistance rises to zero point two two kelvin per watt, the same screening calculation reaches ninety degrees, exceeding our example limit.","speechStart":242.347875,"speechEnd":250.421312},{"start":250.601,"end":254.439,"text":"これは未解決のリスクで、動画上の合格ではありません。","english":"That is an unresolved risk, not an animated pass.","speechStart":250.601313,"speechEnd":254.259229},{"start":254.439,"end":260.664,"text":"モデル版、境界条件、測定位置、不確かさを保存し、持続的な処理速度を確認します。","english":"Preserve model revision, boundary conditions, measurement locations, and uncertainty. Then check sustained throughput.","speechStart":254.439229,"speechEnd":260.484146},{"start":260.664,"end":270.0,"text":"温度制御による速度低下も、検証結果に含めます。","english":"Any performance reduction from thermal throttling belongs in the verification result.","speechStart":260.664146,"speechEnd":264.399583},{"start":270.0,"end":272.203,"text":"最後に全体へ戻ります。","english":"Return to the complete system.","speechStart":270.35,"speechEnd":272.022667},{"start":272.203,"end":276.618,"text":"成果物は、版管理した要件基準と未解決事項の一覧です。","english":"Deliver a versioned requirements baseline and an explicit open-issues list.","speechStart":272.202667,"speechEnd":276.438417},{"start":276.618,"end":282.645,"text":"重要な要件を担当者と検証証拠につなぎ、未測定項目は未検証のままにします。","english":"Link each critical requirement to an owner and its verification evidence; unmeasured items remain unverified.","speechStart":276.618417,"speechEnd":282.465271},{"start":282.645,"end":284.745,"text":"次は機能とダイの分割です。","english":"Next comes functional and die partitioning.","speechStart":282.645271,"speechEnd":284.564792},{"start":284.745,"end":287.593,"text":"要件を候補システム構成へ変換します。","english":"Turn requirements into candidate system compositions.","speechStart":284.744792,"speechEnd":287.413292},{"start":287.593,"end":300.0,"text":"成功の条件を先に定義すれば、後続の製造と試験で何を証明すべきかが明確になります。","english":"Defining success first gives every later manufacturing and testing activity a clear purpose and a claim to demonstrate.","speechStart":287.593292,"speechEnd":293.908625}],"ko":[{"start":0.0,"end":5.536,"text":"첫 번째 활동은 시스템의 역할과 패키지 요구사항 정의입니다.","english":"Welcome to activity one: defining system and package requirements.","speechStart":0.35,"speechEnd":5.355688},{"start":5.536,"end":11.45,"text":"화면의 가속기는 교육용 모델이며 제조 구조는 아직 선택하지 않았습니다.","english":"The accelerator below is a teaching model; its manufacturing architecture has not been selected.","speechStart":5.535687,"speechEnd":11.270021},{"start":11.45,"end":15.662,"text":"결과물은 근거를 추적할 수 있는 요구사항 표입니다.","english":"Our deliverable is a traceable requirements table.","speechStart":11.450021,"speechEnd":15.482042},{"start":15.662,"end":23.642,"text":"무엇을 수행하고, 어떤 조건에서 동작하며, 어떤 증거로 합격을 판단할지 명확히 하세요.","english":"State what the system must do, under which conditions, and which evidence will demonstrate success.","speechStart":15.662042,"speechEnd":23.462458},{"start":23.642,"end":30.0,"text":"멋진 칩 적층 구조가 이 세 가지 답을 대신하지는 못합니다.","english":"An impressive stack of chips cannot replace those three answers.","speechStart":23.642458,"speechEnd":28.334208},{"start":30.0,"end":32.733,"text":"먼저 사용 상황을 기록합니다.","english":"Begin with the use case.","speechStart":30.35,"speechEnd":32.553042},{"start":32.733,"end":38.02,"text":"이 가상의 가속기는 일 초짜리 시연이 아니라 지속적인 처리가 필요합니다.","english":"Our hypothetical accelerator must process a sustained workload, not a one-second demonstration.","speechStart":32.733042,"speechEnd":37.840083},{"start":38.02,"end":45.787,"text":"데이터 크기, 읽기와 쓰기 방향, 최대와 평균 요구량, 허용 지연, 동작 시간을 기록하세요.","english":"Record data size, read and write directions, peak and average demand, allowed latency, and operating duration.","speechStart":38.020083,"speechEnd":45.607354},{"start":45.787,"end":51.051,"text":"높고 짧은 막대는 순간 부하이며 긴 평탄 구간은 지속 부하입니다.","english":"The short tall bars represent bursts; the long plateau represents sustained activity.","speechStart":45.787354,"speechEnd":50.871313},{"start":51.051,"end":53.433,"text":"두 조건을 모두 정의해야 합니다.","english":"Describe both.","speechStart":51.051313,"speechEnd":53.252771},{"start":53.433,"end":60.0,"text":"인터페이스의 최고 속도만으로 실제 응용 성능을 설명할 수는 없습니다.","english":"An interface's headline rate alone does not describe application performance.","speechStart":53.432771,"speechEnd":58.424396},{"start":60.0,"end":65.982,"text":"대역폭, 방열, 크기, 시험에 각각 요구사항 번호를 부여합니다.","english":"Create four requirement identifiers: bandwidth, thermal performance, physical envelope, and test access.","speechStart":60.35,"speechEnd":65.802437},{"start":65.982,"end":72.356,"text":"각 행에는 조건, 단위, 기준값, 검증 방법, 담당자가 필요합니다.","english":"Every row needs conditions, units, a threshold, a verification method, and an owner.","speechStart":65.982438,"speechEnd":72.176271},{"start":72.356,"end":78.714,"text":"대역폭은 단순히 빠르다고 쓰지 말고 한 방향의 유효 데이터 속도로 정의하세요.","english":"For bandwidth, specify useful data rate in one direction, not simply fast.","speechStart":72.356271,"speechEnd":78.534021},{"start":78.714,"end":83.21,"text":"모르는 값은 미정으로 두고 확인 담당자를 지정합니다.","english":"Leave unknown values open and assign responsibility for resolving them.","speechStart":78.714021,"speechEnd":83.03},{"start":83.21,"end":90.0,"text":"제안, 추정, 실측에 따른 합격은 서로 다른 상태로 관리해야 합니다.","english":"A proposal, an estimate, and a measured pass are different states.","speechStart":83.21,"speechEnd":88.960854},{"start":90.0,"end":92.912,"text":"교육용 계산 예를 보겠습니다.","english":"Consider this teaching example.","speechStart":90.35,"speechEnd":92.732271},{"start":92.912,"end":98.73,"text":"한 방향으로 육십사 개 레인이 있고, 각 레인은 초당 십육 기가비트입니다.","english":"Sixty-four lanes in one direction, each carrying sixteen gigabits per second.","speechStart":92.912271,"speechEnd":98.549792},{"start":98.73,"end":102.346,"text":"원시 합계는 초당 천이십사 기가비트입니다.","english":"Raw aggregate rate is one thousand twenty-four gigabits per second.","speechStart":98.729792,"speechEnd":102.166125},{"start":102.346,"end":112.51,"text":"프로토콜과 작업 부하의 종합 효율을 팔십 퍼센트로 가정하고, 바이트로 바꾸기 위해 팔로 나누면 초당 백이 점 사 기가바이트입니다.","english":"Assume eighty percent combined protocol and workload efficiency; divide by eight to obtain one hundred two point four gigabytes per second.","speechStart":102.346125,"speechEnd":112.329813},{"start":112.51,"end":115.071,"text":"규격이 보증하는 값은 아닙니다.","english":"This is not a standards guarantee.","speechStart":112.509812,"speechEnd":114.891188},{"start":115.071,"end":120.0,"text":"효율, 방향, 통신 조건을 별도로 검증해야 합니다.","english":"Verify efficiency, direction, and traffic conditions separately.","speechStart":115.071188,"speechEnd":119.47275},{"start":120.0,"end":123.062,"text":"열도 조건을 명시해 추정합니다.","english":"Start thermal planning with explicit assumptions.","speechStart":120.35,"speechEnd":122.881792},{"start":123.062,"end":132.114,"text":"지속 전력 이백오십 와트, 전체 냉각계의 유효 열저항은 와트당 영 점 일팔 도, 주변 온도는 삼십오 도로 가정합니다.","english":"Assume two hundred fifty watts sustained, an effective resistance of zero point one eight kelvin per watt for the complete cooling system, and thirty-five degrees ambient.","speechStart":123.061792,"speechEnd":131.934271},{"start":132.114,"end":139.007,"text":"집중 정수 정상 상태 추정치는 팔십 도로, 가정한 한계 팔십오 도보다 오 도 낮습니다.","english":"A lumped steady-state estimate gives eighty degrees, five below our illustrative limit.","speechStart":132.114271,"speechEnd":138.827125},{"start":139.007,"end":142.918,"text":"하지만 최고 접합 온도를 검증한 결과는 아닙니다.","english":"That is not verified peak junction temperature.","speechStart":139.007125,"speechEnd":142.738479},{"start":142.918,"end":150.0,"text":"접촉면, 기류, 국부 전력, 과도 상태를 모델링하고 측정해야 합니다.","english":"Interfaces, airflow, local power, and transients still require modeling and measurement.","speechStart":142.918479,"speechEnd":148.678438},{"start":150.0,"end":152.64,"text":"보드 전체로 시야를 넓힙니다.","english":"Pull back to the board.","speechStart":150.35,"speechEnd":152.459979},{"start":152.64,"end":162.065,"text":"이 예에서는 패키지 본체에 가로와 세로 육십 밀리미터, 높이 사 밀리미터를 배정하며 냉각기와 고정 부품은 별도로 계산합니다.","english":"Reserve sixty by sixty millimeters and four millimeters of package-body height in this example; budget the cooler and mounting hardware separately.","speechStart":152.639979,"speechEnd":161.885104},{"start":162.065,"end":168.772,"text":"다이까지의 전원 경로를 그리고 공급 범위, 전압 강하 예산, 측정 지점을 지정하세요.","english":"Trace power into the dies, and specify supply range, voltage-drop budget, and measurement points.","speechStart":162.065104,"speechEnd":168.592062},{"start":168.772,"end":173.041,"text":"작은 패키지가 반드시 작은 시스템을 뜻하지는 않습니다.","english":"A smaller package does not automatically make a smaller system.","speechStart":168.772063,"speechEnd":172.861146},{"start":173.041,"end":180.0,"text":"소켓, 커패시터, 배선, 정비 공간도 배치에 영향을 줍니다.","english":"Sockets, capacitors, routing, and service clearances affect the layout.","speechStart":173.041146,"speechEnd":178.285333},{"start":180.0,"end":184.707,"text":"다이가 가려지기 전에 고장을 관측할 방법을 결정합니다.","english":"Before a die becomes inaccessible, decide how faults will be observed.","speechStart":180.35,"speechEnd":184.527146},{"start":184.707,"end":190.903,"text":"먼저 입고 다이의 시험 증거를 확인하고, 조립 후 연결 및 기능 시험을 계획합니다.","english":"Review incoming die-test evidence, then plan interconnect and functional tests after assembly.","speechStart":184.707146,"speechEnd":190.722979},{"start":190.903,"end":195.959,"text":"화면의 프로브는 제어와 관측 경로를 나타내며 실제 크기는 아닙니다.","english":"The probes symbolize controllable, observable access; their size is illustrative.","speechStart":190.902979,"speechEnd":195.779229},{"start":195.959,"end":200.532,"text":"관측할 수 없는 내부 노드를 정상이라고 가정해서는 안 됩니다.","english":"An unobservable internal node cannot simply be assumed good.","speechStart":195.959229,"speechEnd":200.352438},{"start":200.532,"end":210.0,"text":"고장 범위, 시험 단계, 데이터 책임자를 기록해 비싼 조립 뒤에 시험 전략의 빈틈을 발견하지 않도록 합니다.","english":"Record fault scope, test stage, and data ownership, so expensive integration does not reveal a missing test strategy.","speechStart":200.532438,"speechEnd":208.957896},{"start":210.0,"end":212.548,"text":"이제 후보 구조를 비교합니다.","english":"Now compare candidate architectures.","speechStart":210.35,"speechEnd":212.368375},{"start":212.548,"end":219.506,"text":"실리콘 인터포저, 팬아웃 재배선, 국부 실리콘 브리지는 서로 다른 연결 경로입니다.","english":"Silicon interposers, fan-out redistribution, and local silicon bridges provide different interconnect routes.","speechStart":212.548375,"speechEnd":219.326396},{"start":219.506,"end":223.801,"text":"수직 하이브리드 본딩은 일부 경로와 결합할 수도 있습니다.","english":"Vertical hybrid bonding can also combine with some routes.","speechStart":219.506396,"speechEnd":223.620604},{"start":223.801,"end":228.248,"text":"모두를 모든 제품이 거치는 직렬 공정으로 나열하지 마세요.","english":"Do not turn them into a mandatory serial factory line.","speechStart":223.800604,"speechEnd":228.0685},{"start":228.248,"end":235.207,"text":"유효 대역폭, 전력, 크기, 시험 접근성, 공급 조건, 총비용을 비교합니다.","english":"Compare useful bandwidth, power, dimensions, test access, supply conditions, and total cost.","speechStart":228.2485,"speechEnd":235.026604},{"start":235.207,"end":240.0,"text":"후보를 열어 두고 차이를 입증할 증거부터 정리하세요.","english":"Keep alternatives open while identifying the evidence needed to distinguish them.","speechStart":235.206604,"speechEnd":239.041438},{"start":240.0,"end":242.984,"text":"냉각 가정을 바꿔 보겠습니다.","english":"Challenge the cooling assumption.","speechStart":240.35,"speechEnd":242.804292},{"start":242.984,"end":252.448,"text":"유효 열저항이 와트당 영 점 이이 도로 증가하면, 같은 전력에서도 추정 온도는 구십 도가 되어 사례의 한계를 넘습니다.","english":"If effective system resistance rises to zero point two two kelvin per watt, the same screening calculation reaches ninety degrees, exceeding our example limit.","speechStart":242.984292,"speechEnd":252.267937},{"start":252.448,"end":256.73,"text":"이는 미해결 위험이며 애니메이션상의 합격이 아닙니다.","english":"That is an unresolved risk, not an animated pass.","speechStart":252.447937,"speechEnd":256.550208},{"start":256.73,"end":264.552,"text":"모델 버전, 경계 조건, 측정 위치, 불확실성을 보존하고 지속 처리량을 확인하세요.","english":"Preserve model revision, boundary conditions, measurement locations, and uncertainty. Then check sustained throughput.","speechStart":256.730208,"speechEnd":264.372167},{"start":264.552,"end":270.0,"text":"열에 따른 속도 제한도 요구사항 검증 결과에 포함해야 합니다.","english":"Any performance reduction from thermal throttling belongs in the verification result.","speechStart":264.552167,"speechEnd":269.4655},{"start":270.0,"end":273.212,"text":"마지막으로 전체 시스템을 봅니다.","english":"Return to the complete system.","speechStart":270.35,"speechEnd":273.0325},{"start":273.212,"end":278.541,"text":"결과물은 버전이 있는 요구사항 기준선과 미해결 항목 목록입니다.","english":"Deliver a versioned requirements baseline and an explicit open-issues list.","speechStart":273.2125,"speechEnd":278.360854},{"start":278.541,"end":286.544,"text":"중요한 요구사항을 담당자 및 검증 증거와 연결하고, 측정하지 않은 항목은 미검증으로 남깁니다.","english":"Link each critical requirement to an owner and its verification evidence; unmeasured items remain unverified.","speechStart":278.540854,"speechEnd":286.364312},{"start":286.544,"end":289.453,"text":"다음 활동은 기능과 다이 분할입니다.","english":"Next comes functional and die partitioning.","speechStart":286.544312,"speechEnd":289.273021},{"start":289.453,"end":292.892,"text":"요구사항을 후보 시스템 구성으로 바꿉니다.","english":"Turn requirements into candidate system compositions.","speechStart":289.453021,"speechEnd":292.711813},{"start":292.892,"end":300.0,"text":"성공 조건을 먼저 정의해야 이후 제조와 시험에서 무엇을 입증해야 하는지 분명해집니다.","english":"Defining success first gives every later manufacturing and testing activity a clear purpose and a claim to demonstrate.","speechStart":292.891813,"speechEnd":299.455583}]}}};
